WHAT TO CHECK IN "MY ANALYSIS":
- How much of the data was actually validated vs analyzed.
- Overlap between data used to design the method and data used
  to evaluate it.
- Dataset or vendor/domain bias.
- Dependence on heuristics or manual steps.
- Missing baselines, unclear metric definitions.
- What the method does not cover that the paper itself
  describes as a real problem.
- Whether results were shown on only one case or device.
Mark anything you are unsure about as an observation, not a
fact.

